<section class="sec light" id="why">
<div class="rail l"><span>礼 · 力 · 心</span></div>
<div class="wrap">
<p class="kicker rv">Why judo</p>
<h2 class="rv">Built for kids.<br>Built for adults.</h2>
<div class="why">
<article class="rv"><span class="num">01</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2l3 7h7l-5.5 4.5L18 21l-6-4-6 4 1.5-7.5L2 9h7z"/></svg><h3>Confidence for kids</h3><p>Children not only gain the physical benefits from judo, they also build their self-confidence, discipline, coordination and personality.</p></article>
<article class="rv"><span class="num">02</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 4v16M18 4v16M6 12h12M3 8v8M21 8v8"/></svg><h3>Fitness for adults</h3><p>For adults, judo is an ideal sport to improve fitness and flexibility whilst helping to improve their overall well-being. It pairs well with sports such as rugby.</p></article>
<article class="rv"><span class="num">03</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 22c5-3 8-7 8-12V5l-8-3-8 3v5c0 5 3 9 8 12z"/></svg><h3>The gentle way</h3><p>Judo, meaning “the gentle way”, is a modern Japanese martial art and Olympic sport. It emphasises technique, balance, leverage, and respect.</p></article>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec dark" id="team">
<div class="rail r"><span>先生</span></div>
<div class="wrap">
<p class="kicker rv">Our team</p>
<h2 class="rv">Coaches in your corner</h2>
<p class="lead rv">Our coaches are all experienced, insured, trained in safeguarding and follow BJA’s Child Protection &amp; Vulnerable Adults Policies and Procedures.</p>
<div class="team-wrap">
<figure class="patron rv"><span class="kj" aria-hidden="true">師範</span><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-neil" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop photo of Neil Adams" src="/website/assets/uploads/London_2012_-_Neil_Adams_crop.jpg" credit="Photo: Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA" credit-href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:London_2012_-_Neil_Adams_crop.jpg"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Neil Adams MBE</b><span>Club Patron</span><p>World Champion, twice Olympic silver medallist and five-time European Senior Champion, with a 15-year run of international podium finishes. Neil continues to develop the sport and train young judoka at an elite level. <a href="https://www.neiladamsjudo.info/">neiladamsjudo.info →</a></p></figcaption></figure>
<div class="team">

<figure class="rv"><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-bruce" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop photo of Bruce Newcombe" src="/website/assets/uploads/BM-2-150x150.png"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Bruce Newcombe</b><span>President &amp; Senior Coach</span><p>Joined the club in 1964 aged 11. British Judo Squad 1974–80 and Olympic reservist for Moscow 1980. British Open silver (1978), ten-time Midlands Area Champion and holder of British, All England and All Scotland titles. Coached the Midlands Junior Squad for 19 years, producing four British team titles and national champions including Simon Moss and Paralympic medallist Sam Ingram.</p></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv"><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-josh" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop photo of Josh Giles" src="/website/assets/uploads/20190407_lignano_fdc_day1_terranova_rocco_ita_joshua_giles.jpg" credit="Photo: Franco Di Capua / JudoInside.com" credit-href="https://judoinside.com/judoka/81832/Joshua_Giles"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Josh Giles</b><span>Head Coach</span><p>Coventry born and bred, on the mat here since age 5. British Senior Champion 2018 (-60kg) and a European Open silver (Cluj-Napoca 2022) and bronze (Sofia 2023) medallist for Great Britain, plus European Cup bronze in Sarajevo and a Junior European Cup medal. British U15, Cadet and U21 champion along the way, and English Open champion four times. Josh leads junior and senior sessions.</p></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv"><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-zviad" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop photo of Zviad Tsiklauri" src="/website/assets/uploads/GS_I9801-1662744120-1662744120.jpg" credit="Photo: International Judo Federation" credit-href="https://www.ijf.org/"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Zviad Tsiklauri</b><span>Coach · World &amp; European Champion</span><p>Georgian heavyweight (+100kg) and Veterans World Champion 2017. A British Open bronze medallist (2004, 2009), English Senior Open champion 2013 and 2014, London Senior Open champion 2013 and still winning: gold at the Kent International 2022 and a London Open medal in 2024. Brings Georgian-style gripping and power judo to the club.</p></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv"><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-sara" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop photo of Sara Hayes" src="/website/assets/uploads/Sara-2.jpg"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Sara Hayes</b><span>Club Secretary &amp; Coach</span><p>Practising judo since 1972, the last 25 years in Coventry. Competed at junior and university level and enjoys the technical side of the sport: a first dan, qualified Club Coach and National C Referee. Served on the BJA Complaints &amp; Conduct Commission and on the BJA Board as an independent non-executive member from 2013 to 2016.</p></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv"><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-chloe" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop photo of Chloe Cherry" src="/website/assets/uploads/001-Chloe-2-281x300.jpg"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Chloe Cherry</b><span>Chairman &amp; Club Welfare Officer</span><p>Judo runs in the family. Chloe started at five in Ireland and trained for over ten years, finishing her competitive career representing Ireland on the national team. As Chairman and Welfare Officer she keeps the club safe, welcoming and friendly for every member.</p></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv"><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-lee" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop action shot of Lee Tibbatts"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Lee Tibbatts</b><span>Coach &amp; Technical Specialist</span><p>An experienced judoka with decades on the mat, deeply rooted in the Midlands judo community. Known for exceptional technical precision, he is highly regarded across the region as an outstanding uke for high-level practice and official dan gradings. Trained under world-class mentorship, Lee brings an analytical approach to the club, helping players sharpen their throwing accuracy, standardise their form and prepare confidently for competition and grading milestones.</p></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv"><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-adrian-d" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop action shot of Adrian Drugulescu"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Adrian Drugulescu</b><span>Coach &amp; Groundwork Specialist</span><p>Brings a highly strategic and tactical approach to the coaching team, with a strong emphasis on newaza (groundwork) transitions and submission mechanics. Specialising in linking explosive standing techniques seamlessly into dominant ground control, his training blocks focus heavily on grip fighting (kumi-kata) and breaking opponent tempos. He works closely with the senior squad to cultivate aggressive match-play pacing and resilience on the mat.</p></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv"><div class="belt"></div><div class="pic"><image-slot id="coach-henry" shape="rect" placeholder="Drop action shot of Henry So"></image-slot></div><figcaption><b>Henry So</b><span>Coach &amp; Youth Academy Lead</span><p>Focuses on long-term athlete development, managing the vital transition phase where intermediate and junior squads advance into technical syllabus concepts. His coaching philosophy champions agility, exceptional breakfalls (ukemi), and opportunistic footwork over raw physical strength. Known for his patient and encouraging mentoring style, he excels at building confidence in younger judoka while instilling clean, injury-free foundational habits.</p></figcaption></figure>
</div>
</div>
